{
  "_doc": "DTA class names accepted by object_list / iterate / IsASubclass. Filtering resolves through the shipped `objects` superclass graph, which uses DTA names -- NOT C++ class names. A C++ name yields an EMPTY result, indistinguishable from 'no such objects exist'.",
  "_provenance": {
    "source": "orig-assets/extracted/**/*objects.dta (top-level forms + every (superclasses ...) entry) -- the same data SystemConfig(\"objects\") is built from, so this IS the engine's vocabulary",
    "extracted": "2026-08-02",
    "note": "IsASubclass(child,parent) also returns true when child == parent (Utl.cpp:67), so any literal ClassName works as a filter even if it is absent here -- e.g. UIScreen enumerates the 3 objects whose class is literally UIScreen, while HamScreen appears in no objects.dta at all so {main iterate UIScreen} yields 3, not 296. The real console behaves identically; this is a cross-target invariant, not a native divergence."
  },
